---

<MarketingLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonical={meta.canonical} jsonLd={courseJsonLd}>
  {/* §1 Hero */}
  {/* Mobile spacing here is MEASURED, not eyeballed. On a 375x812 phone the
      original hero pushed the credit line to y=816, i.e. the one sentence that
      explains why both buttons exist started below the fold. Every md: prefix
      below preserves the desktop look while buying that line back on mobile.
      If you edit this hero, re-measure it. */}
  <section class="py-12 md:py-28 px-6" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-cream))">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
      <p class="font-accent text-sm tracking-[0.3em] uppercase mb-4 md:mb-6" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))">Eden's Table</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold leading-tight mb-4 md:mb-6" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">
        Herbalism for the<br /><span class="italic">Whole Family Table.</span>
      </h1>
      <div class="w-16 h-px mx-auto my-5 md:my-8" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))"></div>
      <p class="font-body text-base md:text-lg text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-4 md:mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        A K-12 Biblical herbalism curriculum for homeschool families. Open-and-go lesson plans, memory songs, kitchen labs, garden activities, and a recurring family story, all rooted in Scripture and creation stewardship.
      </p>
      <p class="font-accent text-sm tracking-wider uppercase mb-5 md:mb-8" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-sage))">
        Sprouts (K-2) · The complete 36-week year, in one box
      </p>
      {/* id="early-access" is load-bearing: the homepage links to
          /homeschool#early-access (index.astro). Keep it even though the
          lead-magnet capture that originally lived here is gone. */}
      {/* TWO doors, deliberately. The kit is the commitment and stays the primary
          filled button; the Starter Unit is the lower-commitment way in for a
          reader who is not ready to spend $249 on something that ships in 2027,
          whose only other option is to close the tab.

          They are NOT presented as equals. Same size so neither looks like an
          afterthought, but filled vs outline keeps the kit visually first, and
          the kit sits left / first in the DOM so it is what a screen reader and a
          scanning eye reach first.

          The credit line directly under them is what makes the pair honest rather
          than a fork in the road: choosing the small door costs nothing, because
          the $39 comes off the kit later. Without that sentence the two buttons
          compete; with it they are a sequence.

          data-cta on both so the split is actually measurable in cta_events. The
          hero had no beacons at all before this. */}
      <div id="early-access" class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 scroll-mt-28">
        <div class="flex flex-col items-stretch justify-center gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:gap-4 w-full max-w-xl">
          <a href="#pricing" data-cta="homeschool-hero-preorder" class="inline-flex w-full sm:w-auto">
            <Button variant="eden" size="xl" className="w-full h-full whitespace-normal text-sm sm:text-base leading-snug min-h-[48px] py-3 px-6">
              Preorder the Sprouts Kit · $249
            </Button>
          </a>
          <a href="/starter" data-cta="homeschool-hero-starter" class="inline-flex w-full sm:w-auto">
            <Button variant="eden-outline" size="xl" className="w-full h-full whitespace-normal text-sm sm:text-base leading-snug min-h-[48px] py-3 px-6">
              Start with 6 Weeks Digital · $39
            </Button>
          </a>
        </div>

        {/* The whole point of showing both. Keep the two numbers and the word
            "deducted" together: a reader skimming should be able to take the
            meaning from this one line without reading the rest of the page. */}
        <p class="font-body text-sm max-w-lg mx-auto mt-1 leading-relaxed" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">
          Buy both and the <strong>$39 is deducted from the $249</strong>, so starting
          small costs you nothing.
        </p>

        <p class="font-body text-sm text-muted-foreground max-w-md mx-auto">
          Founding price for the first 500 kits, then $349 retail. Flat $12 shipping per order.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-accent text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-sage))">
          Aiming to ship July 31, 2027 · Guaranteed on or before September 30, 2027
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* §1.5 Why buy an herbalism curriculum (copy doc Section 1) */}
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 px-6 bg-background">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="text-center mb-10">
        <p class="font-accent text-sm tracking-[0.3em] uppercase mb-3" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))">Why this. Why now.</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold leading-tight" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">
          School will teach her the parts of a flower.<br />It will not teach her what the flower is for.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center mb-12">
        <div class="font-body text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-foreground space-y-4">
          <p>I spent years as a credentialed classroom teacher with a Master's in education. I know what is in the standards, and I know what is not. Somewhere in there a child learns to label a stem, a root, and a petal. Nowhere in there does a child learn what to reach for when her throat hurts, what is happening inside her body while it heals, or why any of it was put here in the first place.</p>
          <p class="font-serif text-lg italic" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">That is not a small gap. That is the entire practical use of the subject, left out.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-white shadow-sm border" style="border-color:hsl(var(--eden-gold) / 0.3)">
            <img src="/showcases/ET_WeekAtAGlance.png" alt="Week 5 of the Sprouts Teacher's Guide, showing the calendula week laid out Monday through Friday with the scripture, the kitchen lab supply list, and the subjects woven through the week." loading="lazy" width="1275" height="1650" class="w-full h-auto" />
          </div>
          <p class="font-accent text-xs tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mt-2 text-center" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))">One real week, exactly as it arrives · Week 5 · Calendula</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-cream))">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold mb-3" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">Health stewardship is not a hobby subject.</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Your child is going to live in one body for the whole of her life. She will make decisions about it every single day, starting long before she is grown. Teaching her to understand it, care for it, and pay attention to what it is telling her is not enrichment. It is one of the more practical things you will ever hand her, and we treat it that way, as a subject with a scope, a sequence, and a full year of work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-cream))">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold mb-3" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">One plant a week. Ten subjects come with it.</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">This is not herbalism bolted onto your existing school day. A single week on a single plant carries Bible, science, language arts, math, art, history, geography, Latin, health, and character, and the Week at a Glance page tells you which day carries which. You are not stacking ten subjects into a morning. You are teaching one plant well, and the disciplines arrive with it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-cream))">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold mb-3" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">The year your children are in is the one you have.</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Sprouts is K-2, and it is the first band we are printing. Seedlings, Cultivators, and Practitioners follow it. A child who starts this year grows through the whole sequence with us. A child who waits starts it a year older, in a year we cannot give back.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="text-center mt-10">
        <a href="#pricing">
          <Button variant="eden" size="xl">Preorder the Sprouts Kit · $249</Button>
        </a>
        <p class="font-body text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-3">Founding price for the first 500 kits. Retail is $349.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* §2 Four Grade Bands */}
  <section class="py-16 px-6 bg-background">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold mb-4" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">Four Grade Bands. One Family Vision.</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto">Eden's Table grows with your children, from wonder-filled kitchen labs to clinical reasoning in high school.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5">
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6 border-2" style="border-color:hsl(var(--eden-gold));background-color:hsl(var(--eden-cream))">
          <Sprout className="w-6 h-6 mb-3" color="hsl(var(--eden-gold))" />
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold mb-1" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">Sprouts</h3>
          <p class="font-accent text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-3" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))">Grades K-2</p>
          <p class="font-body text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4 leading-relaxed">Wonder, stories, and simple plant identification. Kitchen labs and memory songs.</p>
          <span class="text-xs font-body px-2 py-1 rounded" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-gold) / 0.15);color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))">Preorder open now</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6 border-2" style="border-color:hsl(var(--eden-gold));background-color:hsl(var(--eden-cream))">
          <BookOpen className="w-6 h-6 mb-3" color="hsl(var(--eden-gold))" />
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold mb-1" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">Seedlings</h3>
          <p class="font-accent text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-3" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))">Grades 3-5</p>
          <p class="font-body text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4 leading-relaxed">Body systems basics, herb profiles, and family dinner discussions.</p>
          <span class="text-xs font-body px-2 py-1 rounded" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-gold) / 0.15);color:hsl(var(--eden-gold))">Coming after Sprouts</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6 border opacity-75" style="border-color:hsl(var(--border))">
          <BookOpen className="w-6 h-6 mb-3 text-muted-foreground" />
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold mb-1" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">Cultivators</h3>
          <p class="font-accent text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-3 text-muted-foreground">Grades 6-8</p>
          <p class="font-body text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4 leading-relaxed">Body pattern thinking, terrain basics, and garden-to-remedy workflows.</p>
          <span class="text-xs font-body px-2 py-1 rounded bg-muted text-muted-foreground">Launches after 2027</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6 border opacity-75" style="border-color:hsl(var(--border))">
          <Users className="w-6 h-6 mb-3 text-muted-foreground" />
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold mb-1" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">Practitioners</h3>
          <p class="font-accent text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-3 text-muted-foreground">Grades 9-12</p>
          <p class="font-body text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4 leading-relaxed">Clinical literacy, materia medica, and real-world application.</p>
          <span class="text-xs font-body px-2 py-1 rounded bg-muted text-muted-foreground">Launches after 2028</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
      {/* The single biggest silent objection on this page. A parent with an eight
          year old reads "Sprouts, Grades K-2", concludes it is not for them, and
          leaves without ever asking. This catches that thought at the exact moment
          it forms and routes it to the answer on /starter, where the case is made
          in full and there is a $39 way to test it. */}
      <div class="mt-10 rounded-lg p-6 md:p-7 text-center" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-cream));border:1px dashed hsl(var(--eden-gold))">
        <p class="font-serif text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-2" style="color:hsl(var(--eden-bark))">
          Children a bit older, and not sure Sprouts is the right place to start?
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-sm md:text-base text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          It usually still is, and the reason is not what most parents expect. Sprouts and
          Seedlings teach <strong>different</strong> plants, so skipping ahead quietly costs
          your child 36 of the 72 they would otherwise finish with.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/starter#older-kids"
          data-cta="homeschool-bands-older-kids"
          class="inline-block font-accent text-xs md:text-sm tracking-[0.2em] uppercase font-bold px-7 py-3.5 rounded-md border-2"
          style="border-color:hsl(var(--eden-forest));color:hsl(var(--eden-forest))"
        >
          Why we say start at Sprouts anyway
        </a>
      </div>

  </section>

  {/* §3 Three Pillars */}
  <section class="py-16 px-6" style="background-color:hsl(var(--eden-forest))">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold mb-6 text-white">Open-and-Go. Family-Style. Faith-Rooted.</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-left mt-8">
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6" style="background-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.08)">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold mb-3 text-white">No Prep Required</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75)">Every lesson includes a parent guide, student workbook, kitchen lab card, and garden activity card. Open and teach.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg p-6" style="background-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.08)">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold mb-3 text-white">Multi-Age by Design</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75)">Lessons are written for the whole family to learn together. Older students go deeper; younger ones grow into it.</p>
        </div>
